@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Knowledge reader credential isolation (local candidate)
+
+Status: implemented and tested with fictional credentials only. Not deployed to the shared daemon; real reader authentication and Next page integration remain unverified.
+
+The daemon and CLI reject startup if `WEKNORA_API_KEY` or `KNOWLEDGE_SYNC_API_KEY` exists in their inherited environment, including an empty value. This check examines names, not values. The daemon receives only the nonsecret `COMPANION_KNOWLEDGE_CREDENTIAL_FILE` path. Status polling does not decrypt credentials.
+
+An authorized read launches `knowledge-worker.js` beside the daemon bundle through private stdio. Its environment contains only Windows runtime/temp paths and loopback proxy exclusions. The worker reads a bounded DPAPI blob, checks the opened file identity, and passes the encrypted blob to its own hidden PowerShell decryptor through stdin. Plaintext returns through that private child pipe and stays in the worker and its own CLI environment. It never returns to the shared daemon, enters argv, or goes into a plaintext temporary file.
+
+Before every operation, the worker checks the current reader-identity endpoint, refusing redirects and oversized responses. It requires key ID 3, tenant 1, tenant scope, precisely the existing single knowledge base, `retrieve` only, `full_access=false`, the existing expiry `2026-11-08T01:25:46Z`, and an unexpired identity. It creates, renews and broadens no credential. Searches explicitly disable vector matching. Conversation/agent and sync writer capabilities are not enabled by this reader.
+
+The existing adapter projects results inside the worker. Known credential text and common encodings are removed before the stdio response; a binary download containing credential bytes is rejected with a fixed error. CLI/decryptor stderr and unknown exception text never cross to the daemon.
+
+Cancellation waits for the worker-owned CLI/decryptor `close`. The parent never forcibly kills the worker. If the deadline passes, it retains ownership and an unknown drain state until a valid settlement plus worker close arrives. An abnormal exit without settlement stays unknown and blocks further reader operations and daemon drain. Do not reinterpret that state as proof all descendants exited. Unexpected OS termination is outside the cooperative cancellation guarantee.
+
+This prevents accidental propagation through Companion child inheritance. It is not an OS account or memory sandbox against another process running as the same user, and does not claim complete memory erasure.
+
+## Verification
+
+- 7 focused test files / 91 tests passed: isolation, existing knowledge adapter, knowledge HTTP, daemon drain, CLI drain, shutdown failure and changelog.
+- Tests use a fictional reader, a generated fictional DPAPI blob, loopback port 0, fake CLI and fake unrelated Creator/IDE child. The real DPAPI file, key, knowledge service, Creator and models were not used.
+- Cancellation verifies fake CLI PID disappearance before settlement. Overflow verifies cooperative cancellation and a separately bounded acknowledgement. A simulated parent deadline verifies the child stays owned/alive until the worker closes it; abnormal worker exit retains unknown.
+- Production build typecheck passed. Full source+test typecheck still reports the pre-existing TS7016 in `tests/stop-previous-daemon.test.ts:2` for the parallel `stop-previous-daemon.mjs` script. This task does not conceal that error.
+- CLI, daemon and worker bundles built with the existing esbuild configuration. The bundled worker rejected an unapproved method before reading a credential. The full build script was not run because its existing final step stops the previous daemon.
+
+## User-local real-key hookup (not executed)
+
+After approving/deploying this candidate and confirming the previous instance has safely exited through the existing guarded flow, use a fresh local PowerShell session. Do not paste a key into Codex, a browser field, argv or a shared process environment.
+
+```powershell
+Remove-Item Env:WEKNORA_API_KEY, Env:KNOWLEDGE_SYNC_API_KEY -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
+$env:COMPANION_KNOWLEDGE_CREDENTIAL_FILE = 'D:/services/weknora/cli/private/pilot-recovery-reader.dpapi'
+# Launch the approved updated Companion bundle using the normal local startup flow.
+```
+
+The configured path refers to the existing user-owned encrypted credential. No new key or grant is needed. The user then performs one bounded read in Next and checks the fixed auth/result status. Status alone can say configured but cannot establish successful authentication or keyword retrieval. If the existing identity has changed or expired, this candidate refuses it; it does not renew or substitute credentials. Real-key hookup and live end-to-end acceptance remain separate from the fictional tests above.
+
+## Checkpoint and rollback
+
+The independent worktree baseline is `3b0c24a`, snapshotting the original shared checkout's parallel changes from HEAD `6ff44f5`. Only the diff after that baseline belongs to this credential task. Shared working files, services and user windows were not changed. Preserve the existing parallel baseline when applying or reverting the candidate; do not reset the shared repository.
